WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
You guys are gonna chew me up and spit me out for this one, but I think men have rights.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.320
I think men have feelings.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.000
I think that men deserve to be heard.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.760
I think that men are indoctrinated by the same systems of oppression that we are,

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.500
and that hating men is still centering men.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.360
Hating men is dehumanizing men.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.740
Hating men is not feminism.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.800
And openly stating that you think men are below you is disrespectful.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.280
So this lady made a video, part of which you just watched,

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.120
and apparently she received so much backlash from her own audience

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.820
that she had to make several follow-up videos explaining and defending what she meant.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.440
And honestly, this is crazy.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.760
We live in a world where someone's saying men have rights, men have feelings,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.180
men deserve to be heard, feels the need to begin with, you guys are going to chew me up and spit

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.200
me out for this one. Think about that. She was not defending some extreme political position. She was

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.260
saying that men are human beings and that openly treating them as inferior is wrong. And yet she

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.320
already knew that even saying this could get her attacked by people within her own community. Now,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.820
to be fair, there were also many reasonable comments underneath her video. A lot of women

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.040
and some men understood exactly what she was saying and agreed with her. But there were

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.360
apparently enough people misrepresenting her words and becoming angry that she felt the need

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.860
to make several more videos clarifying herself. And look, I am making this video to praise her.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:08.360
I probably disagree with this woman on a lot of political and ideological issues, but I respect

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.480
what she did here, because it takes character to challenge your own crowd. It is easy to criticize

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.400
people on the other political side. You already know that your audience will applaud you. It is

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.020
much more difficult to look at people who normally support you and say, uh-uh, no, you are going too

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:25.560
far. This is not acceptable. For most of you watching, saying that men have feelings, rights,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.540
and deserve to be heard is simply common sense. It is the absolute bare minimum and many would

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:33.280
probably consider her point that hating men is dehumanizing and should not be confused with

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.880
feminism fairly reasonable as well. But remember, she is speaking to a community in which for at

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.200
least some people expressing even basic sympathy towards men is apparently treated almost like

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.960
ideological heresy. And that is exactly why voices like hers matter. Because people usually do not

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.640
listen to someone they already consider their enemy. They would most likely not listen to me,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.500
for example. They need to hear these things from somebody they see as being on their own side. So

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.540
yes, as long as there are women like this who are prepared to call out genuine hatred and

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:03.820
dehumanization, even when it comes from their own community, I think there is still some hope.
